Sources
Examples:
Search engines
Public websites
Social media
Public records
DNS information
Job postings

Example
Security tester searches:
Company Name
and discovers:
Email addresses
Technologies used
Employee details

Advantages
Difficult to detect
Low risk

Disadvantages
Limited information

2. Active Reconnaissance
Detailed Definition
Active reconnaissance directly interacts with target systems.
The objective:
"Collect detailed information."

Examples
Port scanning
DNS queries
Banner grabbing

Process
Tester Sends Requests
         ↓
Target Responds
         ↓
Information Collected

Advantages
Detailed information

Disadvantages
Easier to detect

