Module 12: Security Operations Center (SOC)
12.1 SOC Fundamentals

Introduction to Security Operations Center (SOC)
Detailed Definition
A Security Operations Center (SOC) is a centralized team, facility, and process responsible for continuously monitoring, detecting, analyzing, investigating, and responding to cyber security threats within an organization.
A SOC acts as the central defense system of an organization.
The primary objective of a SOC is:
"Continuously monitor systems and quickly detect and respond to security incidents."
SOC teams work 24/7 to identify suspicious activities and prevent security breaches.
SOC monitors:
Networks
Servers
Applications
Endpoints
Cloud environments
Security logs
User activities
Without a SOC:
Security Event
       ↓
No Monitoring
       ↓
Delayed Detection
       ↓
Major Security Breach

Real-world Example
Suppose an attacker attempts:
1000 failed login attempts
SOC systems detect:
Abnormal login activity
SOC analysts investigate and block the attack.

SOC Architecture Overview
Users
  ↓
Applications
  ↓
Logs Generated
  ↓
SIEM Platform
  ↓
SOC Analysts
  ↓
Incident Response

1. SOC Roles
Detailed Definition
SOC teams contain multiple roles, each responsible for different security activities.

Common SOC Roles
SOC Manager
Responsibilities:
Manage SOC operations
Coordinate team activities
Define procedures
Manage incidents

Tier 1 Analyst
Responsibilities:
Monitor alerts
Review security events
Perform initial investigation
Escalate incidents

Tier 2 Analyst
Responsibilities:
Perform deeper investigation
Analyze incidents
Validate threats

Tier 3 Analyst
Responsibilities:
Advanced threat investigation
Malware analysis
Threat hunting

Incident Responder
Responsibilities:
Contain attacks
Remove threats
Restore systems

Threat Hunter
Responsibilities:
Search for hidden threats
Analyze attacker behavior

Real-world Example
Suppose:
Suspicious Login Detected
Tier 1:
Checks alert
↓
Tier 2:
Investigates activity
↓
Tier 3:
Performs detailed analysis
↓
Incident Response Team:
Blocks attacker

2. SOC Workflow
Detailed Definition
SOC workflow describes the sequence of actions followed by SOC teams while handling security events.

SOC Workflow Process
Monitoring
     ↓
Alert Detection
     ↓
Investigation
     ↓
Incident Validation
     ↓
Containment
     ↓
Remediation
     ↓
Reporting

Real-world Example
